(D2b — Discrepancy 2 repro (assembly-failure half): the same map-parameter
 property read, in a program with no float in it, does not assemble —
 `symbol '_file_size' not defined`. That symbol name is the evidence for
 what D2 is: a map parameter's size/length is being compiled into the
 FILE size routine. A float elsewhere in the program links the file
 runtime in, at which point the call resolves and silently returns -1
 (the file-size error value) instead of failing to build.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D2b.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   D2b.asm:72: error: symbol `_file_size' not defined
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)
a map called ages is {"ann": 30, "bob": 40}.

